@startuml sequential-sibling-arena-convention
' ============================================================================
' sequential-sibling-arena-convention.puml — the arena-space vs block-space
' off-by-one that produced "char v2 sequential child mismatch".
' A child's on-disk pointer stores block_id = arena_id + 1 (block 0 is the file
' header). The sequential-sibling PRODUCER read block_id verbatim as the arena
' id; the reader/validator uses the canonical arena_id = block_id - 1. The two
' disagree by exactly one arena, so the writer's own contiguity self-check
' rejected the node.
' Source: §1 of checkpoint-growth-sequential-sibling-fixes.md.
' Color key (persistence palette):
'   blue  #BBDEFB  disk-backed (the on-disk child pointer / arena)
'   teal  #B2DFDB  the overlay serializer's producer decision
'   indigo #C5CAE9 the checkpoint validator / reader
'   red   #FFCDD2 the bug (mismatch)
'   green #C8E6C9 the fix (match)
' ============================================================================
skinparam defaultFontSize 14
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #212121
  BorderThickness 1.3
}

title Sequential-sibling encoding — arena-space vs block-space off-by-one

rectangle "**Child on disk**\nSwizzledPtr::on_disk(block_id, slot)\nblock_id = arena_id + 1\n(block 0 = file header)\n<latex>block\\_id = 1,\\; slot = 148</latex>" as CHILD #BBDEFB

package "PRODUCER — check_sequential_char_children (char/persist.rs)" #F5F5F5 {
  rectangle "**BEFORE (bug)**\narena_id := loc.block_id\n<latex>\\Rightarrow arena = 1</latex>" as BUG #FFCDD2
  rectangle "**AFTER (fix)**\narena_id := loc.block_id − 1\n<latex>\\Rightarrow arena = 0</latex>" as FIX #C8E6C9
}

rectangle "**READER / VALIDATOR**\ncollect_char_child_slots → ptr_to_arena_slot\narena_id := block_id − 1\n<latex>\\Rightarrow arena = 0</latex>" as READER #C5CAE9

CHILD --> BUG
CHILD --> FIX
CHILD --> READER

BUG ..> READER : **first_child.arena = 1**\nvs child_slot.arena = 0\n<b>MISMATCH → "sequential\nchild mismatch"</b>
FIX ..> READER : **first_child.arena = 0**\nvs child_slot.arena = 0\n<b>MATCH → round-trips</b>

note bottom of READER
  Canonical convention (core/swizzled_ptr.rs):
  <latex>arena\\_id = block\\_id - 1,\\quad block\\_id = arena\\_id + 1</latex>
  The byte twin (disk_resolve.rs) always used as_arena_slot() (canonical),
  so it never had the off-by-one — only char/vocab read block_id verbatim.
end note

@enduml
